POS system integration: the files that make POS's packages one system,
which no upstream package ships. Installed by packages/pos-integration.

pam.d/  POS's PAM configuration: system-auth, the stack services
        include; a file for every PAM service in POS (util-linux's login,
        su, runuser, chfn, chsh; shadow's passwd, chpasswd, newusers;
        sudo; cronie's crond; systemd ships its own, and the packages of
        the optional stages theirs: openssh's sshd); and other, which
        denies the rest. Installed into pam's vendor directory
        (/pos/share/pam/pam.d); /etc/pam.d overrides it per service.

os-release  The system's identity (ID=pos), installed as /pos/lib/os-release.
        /usr/lib/os-release and /etc/os-release link to it: an image's
        layout, or pos-fedora, which stands in for Fedora's fedora-release.

presets/  POS's systemd presets (80-pos.preset), read before systemd's
        90-systemd.preset and other presets of the system.

udev/  udev rules that start POS's services for devices:
        99-qemu-guest-agent.rules starts qemu-guest-agent.service when
        the VM has the guest agent's port. Installed into
        /pos/lib/udev/rules.d.

bin/pos-stage  Enables and disables the optional stages: links an image of
        the library (/pos/lib/pos/stages) into /etc/extensions, merges it
        with systemd-sysext and runs sysusers, tmpfiles and ldconfig for
        it. Installed as /pos/sbin/pos-stage.

systemd/  Drop-ins for systemd's units: systemd-sysext.service merges
        over /pos (SYSTEMD_SYSEXT_HIERARCHIES), where the stages go.
